WEBVTT

00:00:00.699 --> 00:00:04.545
Sometimes you want a shell on the worker yourself:

00:00:04.545 --> 00:00:08.698
to look around, run a build, or check an agent's work.

00:00:08.698 --> 00:00:12.774
The worker is an ordinary machine, so you can SSH in.

00:00:13.173 --> 00:00:19.208
Every agent works in its own git worktree, inside the project's dot flightdeck folder.

00:00:19.208 --> 00:00:22.647
Change into it, and you're on the agent's branch.

00:00:23.307 --> 00:00:25.573
But you don't need SSH at all.

00:00:25.573 --> 00:00:29.577
FlightDeck Desktop has shells on the worker built in.

00:00:29.882 --> 00:00:34.909
The Worker tab holds shells on the worker itself, outside any project.

00:00:34.909 --> 00:00:37.637
They keep running when you disconnect.

00:00:38.111 --> 00:00:41.965
Open as many as you need, and show them side by side.

00:00:44.633 --> 00:00:48.686
For an agent's worktree, open a terminal from the sidebar.

00:00:48.686 --> 00:00:51.971
It starts in the agent's folder, on its branch.

00:00:53.408 --> 00:01:02.278
And to edit an agent's files in your editor, Open Worktree in VS Code opens the folder over SSH, right on the worker.
